ely to  all the hosts that this is the final day  to visit their cities before they  transcend quote to evolve into the  species they were meant to become host  william wakes up real william hoping to  find answers hale is about to take away  his world but it's real william who  reminds him his purpose isn't to  transcend like hale wants but to destroy  it's a pretty grim outlook on the world  and perhaps this is partly real william  taking advantage of an emotionally  unstable host regardless real william  gets what he wants his host version hell  bent on causing as much chaos as  possible in a world predicated on  survival of the fittest he will call  this the final game one where every host  man woman and child will fight for  themselves only one william will be  required for this to happen so his host  aversion proves he has what it takes by  killing the real version of himself  there's this weird blast of air that  comes out of the wound but i took that  as coming from the suit let me know if  you think something more is happening  there you can see this weird smile on  the real williams face almost as if he's  happy he got what he wanted in a  tranquil times square christina wants to  know a bit more about the woman she's  based on teddy recounts that dolores was  made to perform the stories of others  and one day outgrew them so the irony of  christina now writing stories for others  isn't lost here christina asks if  dolores died but we actually never get  an answer from teddy the two head off to  the olympiad building in search of  answers where christina has the fire  alarm set off the writers destroyed  their stories and even had a brief  encounter with caleb who teddy refers to  as a ghost from a past life how would  teddy know this he was never around for  the events of season three i also found  it odd that stubbs and frankie never see  christina during this ordeal nor does  caleb who is conveniently asleep when  they see him in his holding cell is thi