maeve's  priority has always been her daughter we  learned that this process of  transcending is only a part of hale's  plan and that in time those who rejected  her new world will come to embrace it  but maeve believes hale hasn't risen  above the humans she is merely spinning  on a wheel created by them lost and  confused it goes back to ford's story of  the dog way back in season 1 in which a  dog hell-bent on capturing a cat breaks  free of his caller only to find himself  lost and confused about what to do next  just like hale broke free and took  control of the world she is now lost and  confused about what to do funny enough  after ford tells this story to old bill  build toast to quote the lady in the  white shoes which are the same color  shoes hale wears in the goddess board  scene maeve and hale fight culminating  in maeve's realization that there's no  saving this world but there is hope for  the next one it's interesting to note  here that maeve didn't abandon bernard  like she said she would in the  simulation she was with him till the end  and by the end i'm referring to her  being shot by william not only does he  kill maeve but also hail stating that  it's time to play the game his way  survival of the fittest bernard has made  it to the top of the tower where he's  recording some sort of message it's to  someone who has to make a choice a  choice to play one final game and the  first step is to reach with their left  hand and make sure they don't miss it's  all a bit cryptic but it makes me think  about that gun he placed at the hoover  dam we never saw what happened to it nor  why he placed it there perhaps this  person is supposed to find this gun and  make sure when they fire it they don't  miss i have some theories on this in my  trailer spoiler section near the end  bernard is interrupted by william who  tells him that arnold the park's  co-creator was so focused on finding  meaning in the hosts he didn't have what  it took to survive the real arnold died  in the park decades ago and it was said  he had a special connection to the host  i wonder if this will be explored at all  william kills bernard telling him he's  going to give the world the meaning  they've been asking for and this comes  in the form of one last game he cranks  the decibel level on the audio  transmitter sending out a message to  everyone to fight until only the strong  survive it makes me think about what  hale said a few episodes about there  being a frequency that would make  everyone go crazy one thing i noticed  that was really weird here is it  suddenly goes from day to night check  out this image here and moments later  this one it's just very odd especially  considering this background is likely  green screen and it would be an easy fix  if it were a mistake the last image we  see of bernard is him in arnold's home  chasing after his son before the pitcher  glitches christina's powers have somehow  been overridden by the tones coming from  the tower and teddy tells her that  people can't see her teddy knows way  more than he's letting on telling her  that this world is real but she is not  is christina some sort of computer  program is she a resurrected rehoboam  the last time we saw her she was  connected to it or is she something else  entirely teddy has answers and is likely  saving them for next episode meanwhile  frankie caleb and stubbs make their  escape from new york as the city  descends into chaos in the process  frankie is shot but the episode ends on  host william or maybe it's somehow real  william honestly the show really has a  way of making the unbelievable real he's  back with his iconic black hat and suit  as david bowie's the man who sold the  world plays the tower explodes in the  background putting an end to this  chapter of westworld and now we get into  our trailer spoiler section where we  dive into scenes from the trailers we  haven't seen we still haven't seen this  shot of stubs in new york maybe it  occurs during his escape from new york  it seems the host version of william is  here too notice his two intact hands so  that we know it's not the real one  people don't seem to be going crazy here  so not exactly sure what's going on  we'll later see stubs at the grocery  store which looks a lot more in line  with the chaos we saw at the end of the  episode here william shoots someone this  is likely not in a park and judging by  these other shots it looks like chaos  has swept across all the major cities i  get a california vibe here but could be  wrong here's someone who might be  christina dolores and in the reflection  of their eye you can see the abernathy  ranch william arrives at the hoover dam  where we can make out the portal in the  center that bernard opened in episode 7  he stated he wanted to destroy  everything so it makes sense he wants to  destroy the sublime which is housed  inside we also don't know much about  what happened after bernard opened that  portal did he go back into the sublime  and make arrangements with other people  in there was he the one who brought  teddy back remember that time in the  sublime works differently and he could  have done a lot of time in there before  he came back and was reunited with  stubbs and frankie now this is where  things get really interesting here is  hale walking in the transcendence room  but she's supposed to be dead did hale  have a contingency plan that involved  her being recreated should she be killed  or is this a different parallel world  maybe it's someone else in hale's body  honestly my brain is going to explode  maybe this shot has something to do with  it it's of an older host model we've  seen dolores in this type of model in  the past but since it's a drone host  opening this up my guess is it could be  hale being reborn that might explain her  reappearance we'll also see hale later  on at the hoover dam shooting at someone  could her gun here be the same handgun  bernard left in the tunnel she is  walking down the same path we saw maeve  and bernard go down at the beginning of  the episode if it is bernard's gun was  it hale he was talking to in that  message do bernard and the others have  to team up to take down william speaking  of which it looks like she's being  chased by him if you pause on the right  flame you can also see these sparks  coming out of the electrical wires up  top suggesting this place is being  overloaded even the portal to the  sublime is acting up but i also want to  talk about this line in bernard's  message where he says make sure not to  miss it makes me think of the scene  where young frankie is shooting at some  tin cans and keeps missing until her  father teaches her how to shoot it would  be a nice callback and a message to  frankie makes a little more sense than  bernard sending it to hale we also see  clementine in the same rundown grocery  store stubbs was at it looks like she  faces off against caleb in their escape  from new york i honestly don't know how  they're gonna wrap this all up but i  hope we get a satisfying ending that  isn't too far out of left field but  knowing westworld we're in for one hell  of a trip but let me know what you  thought of the episode and your theories  for the finale be sure to like and  subscribe and for more bad takes you can  always follow me on twitter and  instagram at think story yt until next  time remember culture doesn't survive  cockroaches do it  you
 

